# GSEER .gitattributes — SQL artifact line-ending determinism.
#
# The migration files (internal/storage/migrations/*.sql) and the
# hardened-deployment scripts (deploy/sql/*.sql) are governance objects:
# their SHA-256 hashes are pinned in the owner register and asserted
# byte-for-byte by internal/storage/migrations/artifacts_test.go
# (TestPinnedMigrationArtifactsMatchRegister /
# TestPinnedDeploymentArtifactsMatchRegister).  go:embed reads these
# files at BUILD time from the checked-out working tree, so a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true converts LF to CRLF, the embedded
# bytes drift from the pinned LF hashes, and the artifact tests fail.
#
# Forcing eol=lf makes Git check out every *.sql file with LF on every
# platform, so the embedded bytes (and therefore the pinned hashes) are
# deterministic across Linux and Windows.  No artifact content is
# altered — only the checkout-time line-ending normalization is pinned.
# The regression is pinned by TestPinnedArtifactsAreLFOnAllPlatforms in
# artifacts_lf_test.go.
*.sql eol=lf
